 associated with hematopoietic cell transplants, underscoring the importance of monitoring and managing potential complications in transplant recipients.\",6\r\n1647,TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOPOYÉTICAS,\"The \"\"TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOPOYÉTICAS\"\" is a medical procedure that involves the transplantation of hematopoietic stem cells, which are blood-forming stem cells, to treat a variety of diseases, including cancers and blood disorders. This procedure may require nutritional support for recovery, as patients often experience malnutrition during the treatment of neoplastic diseases. Additionally, the transplantation can lead to complications, such as hepatic veno-occlusive disease. Overall, hematopoietic cell transplantation is a critical intervention for managing serious health conditions, necessitating careful monitoring and support throughout the recovery process.\",15\r\n2333,EICH CRÓNICA,\"EICH CRÓNICA, o enfermedad injerto contra huésped crónica, es una forma prolongada de la enfermedad que puede manifestarse en el postrasplante tardío. Esta condición aparece generalmente después del día 100 del trasplante y se caracteriza por la aparición de infecciones recurrentes y afectaciones en múltiples órganos. Debido a su naturaleza prolongada, la EICH crónica requiere un manejo médico continuo y cuidadoso para abordar sus complicaciones y mejorar la calidad de vida del paciente.\",5\r\n13781,EICH AGUDA,\"La EICH aguda se presenta en los primeros días postrasplante, afectando principalmente a la piel, hígado e intestino, y requiere tratamiento inmediato con corticoides y otros fármacos.\",4\r\n2149,CORTICOIDES,\"Corticosteroids, commonly referred to as corticoides, are a class of steroid hormones utilized in the treatment of a variety of medical conditions. They are particularly effective in managing acute adrenal insufficiency and serve as anti-inflammatory medications for inflammatory bowel diseases (IBD), often used alongside nutritional support. Key corticosteroids such as dexamethasone, prednisolone, and methylprednisolone are employed to enhance appetite and alleviate nausea in cancer patients, although they are associated with several side effects.\n\nIn the context of IBD, corticosteroids like prednisolone and budesonide play a crucial role in significantly suppressing inflammation during acute episodes. They are also used in high doses to treat conditions such as graft-versus-host disease (GVHD), where they help inhibit the activity of pro-inflammatory prostaglandins and cytokines. However, their use can exacerbate the adverse effects of chemotherapy, including nausea and vomiting.\n\nCorticosteroids are known to impact carbohydrate metabolism, particularly in transplant patients, and may lead to nutritional issues in individuals with chronic respiratory diseases. Additionally, they can cause high potassium loss and are linked to muscle loss and an increased risk of infections in critically ill patients. Despite their effectiveness, the use of corticosteroids in treating symptoms of IBD can be controversial, highlighting the need for careful consideration in their application. They are also utilized in the treatment of conditions such as Graves' ophthalmopathy, where they are administered in intravenous pulses for optimal results.\",15\r\n13782,ENFERMEDAD VENOCLUSIVA HEPÁTICA,\"La enfermedad venoclusiva hepática es un conjunto de síntomas y signos hepáticos que afecta a pacientes que han recibido un trasplante, con una incidencia del 20%. Esta condición puede surgir tras el trasplante y tiene un impacto significativo en la función del hígado.\",4\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3487,PACIENTE,ENFERMEDAD DE INJERTO CONTRA HUÉSPED,Patients may develop graft-versus-host disease after undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation,552\r\n4820,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOPOYÉTICAS,Nutrición parenteral is often necessary for patients who 